"\n" [:option {:value "159388"} "Quadruple Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159400"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159415"} "Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159427"} "Eights, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159436"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159456"} "Lightweight Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159471"} "Single Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159498"} "Quadruple Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159507"} "Coxless Pairs, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159519"} "Eights, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159527"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "158741"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "158870"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "158988"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "159120"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "159297"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "159668"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "159848"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261101"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "319120"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "354078"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19008537"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2012533"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/395"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Double Sculls, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "21 – 27 July 1996"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/718"} "Lake Sidney Lanier, Gainesville, Georgia"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/159486"} "28 from 14 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In addition to being the reigning World and Pan American champions in the women’s double sculls, Canadians " [:a {:href "/athletes/36041"} "Marnie McBean"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36029"} "Kathleen Heddle"] " were also Olympic champions in the coxless pairs and the coxed eights, all of which made them favorites to win the double sculls at the 1996 Summer Olympics.  They were likely to face strong competition from " [:a {:href "/athletes/39157"} "Philippa Baker"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39160"} "Brenda Lawson"] " of New Zealand, the 1993 and 1994 World Champions and the 1995 bronze medalists. Germany, the defending Olympic champions, were represented by " [:a {:href "/athletes/37705"} "Manuela Lutze"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37733"} "Jana Thieme"] ", the latter of whom was a World bronze medalist from 1994. There were two other pairs of recent World medalists at the Games: " [:a {:href "/athletes/38804"} "Irene Eijs"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/38831"} "Eeke van Nes"] " of the Netherlands were the reigning World runners-up, while Bulgaria’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/35927"} "Daniela Oronova"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35916"} "Galina Kamenova"] " were the 1993 bronze medalists."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the opening round, the Australian duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/35322"} "Marina Hatzakis"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35334"} "Bronwyn Roye"] " posted the fastest time, beating Germany and Bulgaria to the finish line. The other heats were won by Canada and the Netherlands, the latter of whom defeated the New Zealanders. The Canadians were more dominant in the semi-finals, winning their heat over four seconds faster than the other victors, Chinese duo " [:a {:href "/athletes/36326"} "Cao Mianying"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36351"} "Zhang Xiuyun"] ". In the final, the Canadians stayed comfortably ahead enough for most of the race that they encountered no serious difficulty winning the gold medal. The Dutch, however, had to battle the Chinese to for silver, a fight that they lost by only 0.37 seconds, which left them settling for bronze instead."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/36041"} "Marnie McBean"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/36029"} "Kathleen Heddle"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/36326"} "Cao Mianying"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/36351"} "Zhang Xiuyun"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/38804"} "Irene Eijs"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/38831"} "Eeke van Nes"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/35322"} "Marina Hatzakis"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/35334"} "Bronwyn Roye"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/37733"} "Jana Thieme"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/37705"} "Manuela Lutze"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right